_Balance_ is an important aspect of any game.  A game is not fun if it
only involves going through motions and no risk or suprise occurs.

Below are some of the things I believe are damaging the game balance in NH.
I am not advocating that they be removed from the game, just pointing out
that they can upset balance.

	1. Resistance.  As in fire resistance, etc.  These effects means that
		the game gets EASIER as the player progresses.

	2. Monsters based on player level.  This discourages a player from
		increasing level (eg. the nurse stuff I've heard of).  It
		also distorts the realism of the game.

	3. Wishing for powerful objects.  Quest-type objects can be wished
		for.  This devalues the quest, and forces other parts of
		the game to distort.


My suggestions for rebalancing these effects are:


        1. All resistances/outside-gained-intrinsics wear off, or 
                take player action/inaction to maintain (eg.  ESP lost
                by homicide/elvicide).  This drives the player to
                maintain resistances.  

	2. Have low level monsters less likely to carry powerful objects
		(reducing gain in staying on lower levels).  This drives
		the player downward.  (have monster level based on dungeon
		level).

	3. Have different wishpower for different objects.  The WoW in
		the castle would be powerful, but those found randomly
                generally weak (you wish for 3 potions of extra healing).
		Wishes from genies and water trolls be based on the player
		level [reasoning:  the wish granter will not grant a
		powerful wish to some wimp they could bash, but would
		be more fearsome and submissive to powerful players] 

